## CLI Usage & Examples

Curated command catalog: the main commands grouped by area, with practical
examples. For I/O conventions, project configuration and the always-current
generated command reference, see `context/instructions/reference.md`.

## Agent tooling

- `sdt context new --type <t>` — create a work file ({{.NewTypes}})
- `sdt context path --type <t> [--slug]` — print a path ({{.PathTypes}})
- `sdt context list --type <t>` — list existing files ({{.ListTypes}}); filter with `--status`, a date range and `--where` (see Context queries)
- `sdt context search <query>` — ranked fulltext search over the same corpus; takes the same query filters as `list`
- `sdt context status get|set` — read/update a document's status (per-type
  vocabularies in the status matrix: `context/architecture/stack.md`)
- `sdt context get <doc> [<key>…]` — read a document's frontmatter: the raw
  block when no key is given, else one value per top-level key (no nested keys)
- `sdt context set|unset <doc> <key> [<value>]` — write/remove any top-level
  frontmatter key with byte fidelity (comments, order, quoting preserved);
  `--raw`, `--append`, `--remove` (both YAML list shapes are read and the key's
  existing shape is kept; an unreadable non-empty value is refused);
  `status`/`updated` validated, CLI-owned
  `uid`/`analysis_id`/`plan_id` refused without `--force`
- `sdt q get|set|del <file> <path>` — query/patch a JSON file by gjson path
  (e.g. `sdt q get context/index.json 'documents.#(kind=="analysis")#.path'`)
- `sdt context rename <ref> --slug <new>` — move a document to a new slug
- `sdt context task add ["<step>"] [--phase <n>] [--stream <label>]` — task checklists
  (one file per plan by default, phases as `## Phase` sections)
- `sdt context template --type <t>` — print the per-type instruction file
- `sdt context docs` — generated command documentation
- `sdt context reindex` / `sdt context lint [path...]` — regenerate `index.md` /
  validate the corpus, or only the positional document paths; `--security` adds
  the advisory security scan to the selected scope. Paths must be in the
  corpus-scanned directories; wiki pages use `sdt context wiki lint`.
- `sdt agent roles show|init|check` — list the closed role register; generate the role profiles under `context/roles/`; validate profile set, drift and owned-path overlap
- `sdt agent doctor` — read-only workspace health; `sdt agent verify` — instruction contract; `sdt agent gate` — Build→Vet→Lint→Test
- `sdt template --tmpl` — render Go templates from JSON/YAML data
- `sdt extract --type urls|emails|ips|json-blocks|code-blocks|dates`
- `sdt env parse|get|set|merge` — .env handling
- `sdt diff --a A --b B --diff-format unified|json-patch`

## Logging

`sdt` writes logs to stderr; stdout carries only the command result. Log
format is independent of the result `--format`:

- `--log-format text` (default) — console handler (tinted via
  `github.com/lmittmann/tint`); level and values are coloured on a terminal.
- `--log-format json` — one structured record per line.
- Colour is used only on a TTY; `--no-color` and the `NO_COLOR` environment
  variable force plain text.
- `--quiet` raises the level to `Warn`, hiding info/progress while keeping
  warnings and errors.

## Context queries

`sdt context list` and `sdt context search` share one filter engine
(`internal/ctxquery`): every filter is conjunctive (AND), and both commands
return the same document set for the same filter.

Date range:

- `--after <when>` / `--before <when>` — dated on/after or on/before;
  `--since`/`--until` are aliases.
- `--last <N><unit>` — relative window, exclusive with `--after`; units
  `m` minutes, `h` hours, `d` days, `w` weeks (months/years unsupported).
- `--date created|updated` — reference timestamp (default `created`).
- `<when>` accepts `YYYY-MM-DD`, RFC3339, `now` and `now-<N><unit>`.

Frontmatter filters:

- `--type <k>` — frontmatter `kind` (on `search`; `list` is already scoped to a
  directory by `--type`).
- `--status <s>` — frontmatter `status`.
- `--where <key>=<value>` / `--where <key>!=<value>` — repeatable, any
  frontmatter field.

`--where` matching:

| Field | Matches when |
|-------|--------------|
| scalar | value equals the field (exact, case-sensitive) |
| list | value is a member of the list |
| boolean | value is the literal `true` or `false` (no bare-key form) |
| absent key | never for `=`, always for `!=` |

```
sdt context list --type plan --status active --last 7d
sdt context list --type analysis --where categories=refactor
sdt context search "filter engine" --date updated --after 2026-09-01
```

## Encoding & hashing

- `sdt b64|b32|b64url|hex|url|html [dec]` — encode/decode
- `sdt sha256|sha1|sha384|sha512|md5` — hashes
- `sdt bcrypt|bcrypt verify`, `sdt hmac --key`, `sdt keypair`, `sdt sign|verify`, `sdt cert inspect|expiry`

## Data & conversion

- `sdt conv --in json|yaml|toml|csv|msgpack --out ...`
- `sdt json pretty|minify|valid`

## IDs, time, strings

- `sdt uid v4|v7|nano|ks`, `sdt time unix|iso|http`
- `sdt string uppercase|lowercase|titlecase|count|escape|unescape|replacespace`
- `sdt regexp|regexp replace --expression`

## Network

- `sdt http`, `sdt ipinfo`, `sdt nslookup`, `sdt dns --host --type A|AAAA|MX|TXT|CNAME|NS|PTR`, `sdt port`

## Other

- `sdt gzip|gunzip`, `sdt password`, `sdt qrcode|qrcode read`, `sdt totp uri|code|verify`, `sdt vman`, `sdt config get|set`, `sdt version`

## Examples

```
echo "hello" | sdt b64                                  # encode
echo "password" | sdt sha256                            # hash
echo "payload" | sdt hmac --key "secret"                # hmac
echo '{"a":1}' | sdt conv --in json --out yaml          # convert
echo '{"user":"Alice"}' | sdt template --tmpl "Hi {{"{{"}}.user}}"
cat llm_response.txt | sdt extract --type urls
cat config.yaml | sdt conv --in yaml --out json
echo "password" | sdt sha256 | sdt hex                  # pipeline
sdt diff --a old.json --b new.json --diff-format json-patch
sdt totp code --secret BASE32SECRET
sdt dns --host example.com --type A --format json
sdt context lint context/plan/example.md                    # validate one document
sdt context lint plan/example.md --format json              # context-relative path
sdt context lint --security                                 # corpus + security scan
```
